  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14108748",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-122325",
      "knowledge_point_id": "550bb33b-c427-5667-977d-56ff8c6b458e",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Displacement of a Particle as a Function of Time",
      "problem": "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x$ meters, the velocity is given by $v(x)={e}^{-2x}\\,m/s.$ Initially, $P$ is at the origin $O.$ Find $x$ as a function of time $t.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14108748/assets/8faba5a783797f7025f51ec1ae587cb68355dff7138278689346c2f713275562.png)\n\nWe're given that the velocity function $v(x)$ is\n\n$$\nv(x)={e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nWe know that $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ Therefore, we have the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nSeparating the variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{-2x}}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{2x}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x} & =t+K \\\\ {e}^{2x} & =2t+C \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+C) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=0$ when $t=0.$ Therefore, $C=1,$ and the particular solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1).\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)=2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2)",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4t+1)",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x(t)={t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+2)",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
